  "explains": "fetchSettlementSummary in src/modules/billing/api.ts changes. It calls apiGet with SETTLEMENT_SUMMARY_URL, a constant that endpoints.ts writes over two lines (the name on the first line, the string \"/api/billing/settlements/summary\" on the second); a one-line pattern would miss it. The URL has the segments api, billing, settlements, summary. In acme/api the router tree gives two candidate routes: GET /api/billing/settlements/summary (literal summary) and GET /api/billing/settlements/{settlement_id}. The literal route is the more specific match and wins, so the http edge goes to GET /api/billing/settlements/summary, with evidence at the client line and at the route decorator plus the three include_router lines that compose the full path (/api + /billing + /settlements + /summary). Only SettlementsPage imports fetchSettlementSummary, mounted at /billing/settlements. InvoiceListPage, InvoiceDetailPage import other names from the same api.ts, so named-export narrowing excludes them.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "caller",
    "screen",
    "http_edge"
  ],
  "must_find": [
    {
      "type": "changed_symbol",
      "repo": "acme/web",
      "path": "src/modules/billing/api.ts",
      "symbol": "fetchSettlementSummary"
    },
    {
      "type": "caller",
